# This is just an example. Do not use.

# Gates HTTP Basic Auth on the dashboard (port 55123). Leaving either blank
# disables auth (fail-open) and serves the dashboard unauthenticated.
ADMIN_USER=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=password

# GitHub PAT used by the dashboard's "workspaces" tab to list and clone repos
# into the workspace. Classic PAT with `repo` scope (private + public repos),
# or `public_repo` if only public repos are needed. Leaving this blank
# disables the workspaces tab's GitHub integration (it renders a
# disabled/error state).
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_blahblahblah

# Postgres, used both by the `postgres` infra service itself (POSTGRES_USER/
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD/POSTGRES_DB — the official postgres image's own env vars,
# see services/postgres/compose.yml) and by the healthcheck dashboard's own
# connection (all five vars, read directly by healthcheck/db.go). POSTGRES_HOST
# is the in-container service name ("postgres", reachable by DNS on
# homelab-net) — not "localhost". POSTGRES_DATABASE must match POSTGRES_DB.
# Leaving these unset/unreachable doesn't crash the dashboard: DB-backed
# features (the workspaces tab's persisted list) degrade with a reason
# instead, same as a missing GITHUB_TOKEN above.
POSTGRES_HOST=homelab
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DATABASE=homelab
POSTGRES_DB=homelab
POSTGRES_USER=homelab
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=password

# Caps a single agent run's spend (claude's own --max-budget-usd flag,
# healthcheck/agentprocess.go). Optional; defaults to "1.00" if unset.
AGENT_MAX_BUDGET_USD=1.00

# Shared secret the PreToolUse approval hook (healthcheck/agentprocess.go) uses to
# authenticate callbacks from a claude subprocess back to the dashboard's own HTTP
# API — never generated or set by code, only ever read via os.Getenv. Generate a real
# random value yourself, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Leaving this unset doesn't
# crash the dashboard: the approval hook is simply never attached to agent runs (never
# treated as a valid credential just because an unset value would trivially "match"),
# so gated actions (git commit/push, rm -rf, ...) execute unattended same as before
# Approvals existed, rather than a hook nobody could ever authenticate against.
AGENT_HOOK_SECRET=change-me-generate-a-real-random-value

# Docker socket mounted read-only
# Enable for the dashboard's infra-services list
DOCKER_SOCK_PATH=.

# --- VPN (wg-easy + cloudflared), server-only. See docs/vpn.md. ---
# These placeholders only satisfy `docker compose config`. Real values live in the
# deploy ENV secret / the server's .env — never commit real ones.
#
# Uncomment on the server to start the wireguard + cloudflared services (both are
# gated behind the `vpn` compose profile and stay off in local dev):
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=vpn

# WireGuard endpoint hostname: a DNS-only (unproxied) record on the home public IP,
# SEPARATE from the proxied admin-UI hostname. wg-ddns keeps its A record in sync.
WG_HOST=wg.example.com
WG_UDP_PORT=51820
WG_UI_PORT=51821
WG_DEFAULT_DNS=1.1.1.1
WG_ALLOWED_IPS=0.0.0.0/0
# Optional: exactly one LAN IP allowed through the VPN's RFC1918 block (e.g. the homelab
# server itself, to reach the dashboard over the tunnel). Every other LAN host stays
# unreachable. Leave blank to keep the VPN a pure internet-exit tunnel with zero LAN access.
WG_LAN_ALLOW_HOST=
# bcrypt hash of the wg-easy admin password (generate per docs/vpn.md)
# Note: single quotes are important here or '$' chars can cause problems
PASSWORD_HASH=
# Cloudflare Tunnel token (Zero Trust > Networks > Tunnels)
TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# Cloudflare API token for wg-ddns, scoped Zone:DNS:Edit on the zone (see docs/vpn.md)
CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN=
# Optional: zone name for wg-ddns; derived from WG_HOST when blank
CF_ZONE_NAME=
# Optional: seconds between wg-ddns IP checks (default 60; only hits Cloudflare on change)
DDNS_INTERVAL=60
# Optional: seconds between forced Cloudflare drift checks (default 21600 = 6h)
DDNS_RECONCILE_SECONDS=21600
